// Rule: [T1176] Jewelbug - Com Microsoft Runedge Native Messaging Host
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1176
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR /
// Required telemetry: DeviceRegistryEvents
// Purpose: Source-observed Chrome native-messaging host used to bridge a malicious browser extension to a Windows command helper.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceRegistryEvents for com microsoft runedge native messaging host using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: The endpoint recorded activity against the exact campaign-specific native-messaging host path and requires immediate provenance review.
// A match does not prove: Malicious manifest/helper content, extension load, command execution, C2 activity, data theft or Jewelbug attribution.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint registry events on Windows
// Evidence: Symantec observed Jewelbug writing the Chrome native-messaging host
// key HKCU\SOFTWARE\Google\Chrome\NativeMessagingHosts\com.microsoft.runedge.
// This exact campaign artifact is a triage lead, not attribution proof.
DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith @"\SOFTWARE\Google\Chrome\NativeMessagingHosts\com.microsoft.runedge"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    ReportId,
    ActionType,
    RegistryKey,
    RegistryValueName,
    RegistryValueType,
    RegistryValueData,
    PreviousRegistryValueData,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    InitiatingProcessUniqueId
| order by Timestamp desc
